{"skill":{"slug":"notion-api","displayName":"Notion API Tools"},"version":{"version":"1.1.0","createdAt":1769548782805,"changelog":"- Updated Notion API version header to default to 2025-09-03.\n- Documentation improvements and minor clarifications in SKILL.md.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1386,"sha256":"7b84c73524a1d29d79194e78c4ff2c49a8c967cdfb5ec6f9a47d70cfa69607be","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/notion-api.mjs","size":7205,"sha256":"d0d15b63b1c9b756eeb92df4938993850bcbd41885c959673cb9b217c55d2662","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1951,"sha256":"8855e87a2aab344456453c5364a2be24d3ec26ad30f1414e0128fb5b610302df","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789021581437,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"39a75f33bc875179732ea89446087e2e4deb1de166b7b15287719363c97451be","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/39a75f33bc875179732ea89446087e2e4deb1de166b7b15287719363c97451be","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: notion-api\nVersion: 1.1.0\n\nThe skill bundle provides a Node.js CLI for the Notion API, allowing search, querying, and page creation. It securely handles API keys by reading from environment variables or a standard configuration file (`~/.config/notion/api_key`), and all network requests are directed to the legitimate Notion API endpoint (`https://api.notion.com/v1/`). The `SKILL.md` documentation is purely descriptive and does not contain any prompt injection attempts. The code uses only built-in Node.js modules and shows no evidence of data exfiltration to unauthorized destinations, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or obfuscation.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160057917},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":69,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":16,"checkedAt":1789021581437},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This Notion CLI is mostly purpose-aligned, but it includes under-documented commands that can modify Notion blocks immediately.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Reading NOTION_KEY or a configured local key file and calling api.notion.com are proportionate for a Notion API CLI, but they grant access according to the user's Notion integration permissions.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact contains a Markdown skill file and a dependency-free Node script; no install hooks, package installs, remote payload loading, or tool replacement were found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The main SKILL.md command documentation omits append-blocks and update-block, and mutating commands do not include confirmation, dry-run, or explicit safety guidance.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No cron jobs, startup scripts, background workers, memory writes, or persistent state creation were found; the script only reads a token source when invoked.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose covers Notion search, database queries, and page creation, while the script also implements block retrieval, child listing, block append, and block update operations.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable giving the agent a Notion integration token that can read or modify whatever pages and databases are shared with that integration. Review the block append and update commands before use, and prefer a limited Notion integration or test workspace because mutations happen immediately.","findings":"[LP3] expected: The skill needs network access and a Notion token for its purpose, but the artifact does not provide a narrow permission declaration; this is a reviewability concern rather than evidence of abuse.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The create, append, and update operations can modify remote Notion content without a confirmation or dry-run step, which is material for an agent-invoked skill.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: The script help lists update-block, but the top-level skill documentation and description do not clearly disclose block update capability.\n[RA2] unexpected: The persistence claim was not supported by artifact evidence; I found no scheduled tasks, startup hooks, long-running workers, or state-file writes.\n[E1] expected: Outbound requests go to the official Notion API endpoints needed for search, query, page creation, and block operations; I found no unrelated destination.\n[SDI-1] unexpected: The implemented block editing commands exceed the capability set described in the SKILL.md frontmatter and command documentation.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789021581437}}}}}